<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">
  <PropertyGroup>
    <TargetFramework>net8.0</TargetFramework>
    <PackageId>BulletMLLib</PackageId>
    <Version>5.1.2</Version>
    <Title>BulletMLLib</Title>
    <Authors>dmanning23</Authors>
    <description>Library for parsing BulletML xml files. Used for scripting bullet patterns in shmup games.</description>
    <PackageProjectUrl>https://github.com/dmanning23/BulletMLLib</PackageProjectUrl>
    <PackageLicenseExpression>MIT</PackageLicenseExpression>
    <RepositoryUrl>https://github.com/dmanning23/BulletMLLib</RepositoryUrl>
    <RepositoryType>git</RepositoryType>
    <PackageTags>monogame</PackageTags>
    <GeneratePackageOnBuild>true</GeneratePackageOnBuild>
    <IncludeSymbols>true</IncludeSymbols>
    <SymbolPackageFormat>snupkg</SymbolPackageFormat>
    <GenerateDocumentationFile>true</GenerateDocumentationFile>
    <PackageReadmeFile>README.md</PackageReadmeFile>
    <PackageReleaseNotes>
5.1.2

Duplicate labels are rejected. Two action, bullet or fire nodes with the same label used to load, and a ref silently used whichever came first in the file. ParseXML now throws, pointing at the second one:
Error reading "Content/boss.xml": Duplicate action label "shoot", first used on line 7 (line 10, column 3)
- Labels only need to be unique within a type, so an action and a bullet can still share a label.
- A pattern that relied on the first-match behavior will now fail to load.

Upgrading from 5.0? 5.1.0 made pattern validation much stricter. See the full release notes before upgrading.

Full release notes: https://github.com/dmanning23/BulletMLLib/blob/master/CHANGELOG.md
    </PackageReleaseNotes>
  </PropertyGroup>
  <ItemGroup>
    <None Include="../README.md" Pack="true" PackagePath="" />
  </ItemGroup>
  <ItemGroup>
    <PackageReference Include="MonoGame.Framework.DesktopGL" Version="3.8.*">
      <PrivateAssets>All</PrivateAssets>
    </PackageReference>
    <PackageReference Include="Vector2Extensions" Version="5.*"/>
    <PackageReference Include="Equationator" Version="5.*"/>
  </ItemGroup>
</Project>